# Dev convenience for a test rig. Copy to `firmware/.env` (gitignored) and fill
# in; `make fw-build`/`fw-flash` source it and, with the `dev-credentials`
# feature they turn on, `build.rs` turns these two into compile-time values
# that seed NVS on a device with no credentials of its own. `make fw-release`
# never reads this file and never compiles them in.
#
# They are a shortcut for flashing a bench board, not a deployment mechanism:
# anything saved through the setup page wins, the password is never logged or
# returned by the API, and a build without this file simply has no default.
#
# NEVER commit a filled-in .env.
OPENDMD_WIFI_SSID=your-network
OPENDMD_WIFI_PASS=your-password
